{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Lane f041: change 3038 has LLM-Review +1. CI run 39177510265 `pip-audit` FAILED with \"verdict: BLOCKING — this change touches the dependency map\". `scripts/dependency_audit.py` treats ANY edit to `pyproject.toml` as touching the dependency map (file-level, deliberate). The lock closure carries about 18 HIGH advisories: mcp 1.29.0; pydantic-ai-slim 1.107.2; pyjwt 2.13.0, including PYSEC-2026-4146 with no fix published; urllib3 2.7.0; virtualenv 21.7.4. These are tracked on main by unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis.\nThis change's pyproject hunks are build-only: the editor_assets artifacts glob, 2 `**/node_modules` excludes, the `e2e` marker, and a noqa comment. In a scratch check with those hunks reverted, the wheel still builds with 0 editor_assets entries. Dropping them would unblock Verified but leave the AC grep's `pyproject.toml` hits (editor_assets, prompt_authoring) for a follow-up. This needs an operator decision; no force was used."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792368233307407756,"uuid":"2c5c460b-3036-4224-969d-85389272ef1b"}